    {
      "id": "claim_b33f5d6092f5444993d723b3d263edff",
      "statement": "Alerting has two independent paths onto one backlog item, titled 'Prod backup: failed or stale'. Path one is the run's own failure: backup.sh exits 1 and OnFailure=homelab-backup-alert@%n.service on homelab-backup.service runs backup-alert.sh failed <unit>, with a run killed by TimeoutStartSec=2h reported as hung rather than failed (a whole run measures 8-10 min). Path two is a separate 6-hourly staleness timer and service running backup-staleness.sh, which reads the newest homelab snapshot from the backup repository itself and alerts stale past 36 h, or staleness-unreadable when it cannot read the age at all — 'could not tell' is never reported as fresh. Neither the alert unit nor the staleness service declares OnFailure=, so a failing alert does not recurse and a stale check is not double-reported.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/backup/backup-staleness.sh",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:403ac4d20a966bbca9362c734d8b6d1bcc577c299bfaf43613499b0afddcfe78"
