    {
      "id": "claim_4df3f23a8d494da286afc1250a52f748",
      "statement": "The second alerting path exists precisely because a run that never happens, a hung run, or an upload that silently did nothing fires no OnFailure; a heartbeat written by the run being checked would not be independent, and a CI-hosted check would need the restic password that decrypts every backup in Actions secrets. MCM_BACKUP_STALE_HOURS exists for tests only and no unit sets it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/backup/backup-staleness.sh",
