    {
      "id": "claim_854a4a3a343f4e6aa73e4c26e7c768c4",
      "statement": "backup-alert.sh puts every backup event on exactly one backlog item: it searches open issues for the exact title 'Prod backup: failed or stale' (no label filter, since an unknown label name is silently ignored), comments when the item exists and creates it labelled type/bug and priority/p1 by label id when it does not, never closes it, and a fully good run posts a recovered comment that no-ops when nothing is open.",
      "evidence": [
