    {
      "id": "claim_793015c5a7d84281bc64b2b811ba4afc",
      "statement": "backup.sh holds no secret: the restic password comes from RESTIC_PASSWORD_FILE outside the script, the forge package token is read from a mode-600 file on disk, and every other credential (the Komodo Postgres user and password, the Mongo URIs) is read live from a compose env file or a running container, so no credential is ever assigned a literal in the committed script.",
