    {
      "id": "claim_c059613feef8458884f30790fd2357bb",
      "statement": "The accepted gap in the alerting is that if the whole host, or the prod user's systemd manager, is down, both timers stop and the staleness check goes down with the backup. That is accepted rather than engineered around because the same state stops the forge, the application and every CI run, so it is loud rather than silent; what the two paths cover is the case that went unseen for three months, where the host is up and the backup is broken.",
      "evidence": [
