    {
      "id": "claim_9791198156314d7c836c02b4822603fc",
      "statement": "The backup scripts are guarded behaviourally rather than by inspection, and the guards run in guardrails.yml's naming job, whose node --test scripts/__tests__/*.test.mjs step picks them up automatically. backup-script.test.mjs runs backup.sh against a fake host (docker, restic, curl, systemctl and df shimmed; tar, gzip and python3 real) and pins the measured failure modes, including that a failing forge dump still runs every other dump and still calls restic backup, the per-dump format and minimum verdicts, the eight forge-data excludes, shrink and ack-shrink, staging under ~/backup with tmpfs refused, --group-by host,tags on forget, and the absence of a literal credential; backup-units.test.mjs pins the unit wiring; backup-alert.test.mjs pins the exact forge API calls and the token never appearing in argv; backup-staleness.test.mjs pins 'unreadable is never fresh'; backup-install-manifest.test.mjs pins the committed manifest against the directory; and komodo-cron-retention.test.mjs pins the purge job as hourly, idempotent and touching only its own table.",
