          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:92e7fd9f3e829e3a50fc39764db75b9058ab4d627de4fe5f4b1524c75a32fe85:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4c45bfab41d04a80b6f8b02308d4a077",
      "statement": "The forge-data format check is a content check rather than only a listing check: the tar must list git/repositories/, gitea/conf/app.ini and gitea/jwt/, because a restore without the JWT signing keys changes every issued token and the Actions OIDC identity. The eight --exclude paths are pinned by backup-script.test.mjs, so adding or removing one is a deliberate decision about what a restore loses.",
      "evidence": [
