    {
      "id": "claim_723f2581d00949f2b153c54d48eefb66",
      "statement": "The komodo dump carries a maximum of 500 MB: exceeding it is not a failure but a warn-max verdict, which raises a komodo-oversize alert naming the dump and both sizes, still uploads the snapshot, and suppresses the recovered note so it cannot close the item the oversize alert just opened. The dump also excludes cron.job_run_details' rows (roles come from pg_dumpall --globals-only, each database psql lists from pg_dump --exclude-table-data). Separately, komodo-cron-retention.sql stops the table itself growing by installing the hourly pg_cron job purge-cron-run-history at 17 * * * *, which deletes runs older than 3 days; the file is applied by hand, safe to re-apply because it unschedules the job by jobid before creating it, and touches no other table.",
