    {
      "id": "claim_2c52af8fbda14ff396f1bcb22871a8de",
      "statement": "The install/verify contract rests on three host tokens, each created in the forge UI for this host alone with exactly one scope: ~/backup/forge-issue-token (issue read and write) for backup-alert.sh, ~/backup/forge-package-token (package read) for the release-apks dump, and ~/.config/mcm-forge-read-token (repository read) for the ~/mcm-main checkout, which clones through a credential helper so the token never enters the URL, argv or .git/config. MCM_FORGE_URL in ~/backup/alert.env names the forge as the host reaches it for both the alert and the APK dump, and the real host is never committed.",
