    {
      "id": "claim_71a5072b23fa4e2f8db246b76bd7a0a5",
      "statement": "backup-alert.sh's reason vocabulary is closed — failed, hung, stale, staleness-unreadable, shrink, komodo-oversize, recovered — and an unknown reason exits 2 before any network call. The exit contract is 0 for delivered or nothing to do, 2 usage, 3 not configured (missing or non-600 token file, unset MCM_FORGE_URL) and 4 for a failed forge API call; exits 3 and 4 print 'alert NOT delivered' to the journal instead of failing silently, and only the failed reason consults the unit state, reporting a unit whose Result= is timeout as hung.",
