    {
      "id": "claim_b8dc115b7ef04935bc291dac3339d5ba",
      "statement": "The once-after-install proof that the alerting works is an induced failure: point the run at a repository that does not exist with systemctl --user set-environment RESTIC_REPOSITORY=..., start homelab-backup.service, expect exit 1 and an 'alert delivered' line on the alert unit, and restore the default on the same line — an interrupted override stays set and every nightly fails until it is cleared with systemctl --user unset-environment RESTIC_REPOSITORY. The staleness path is exercised the same way with MCM_BACKUP_STALE_HOURS=0, which must produce an exit 1 and a stale comment on the same item.",
